# Materialized SKOS inverse links
#
# SKOS defines hasTopConcept/topConceptOf and broader/narrower as inverse
# pairs. They are asserted in both directions here because the browser and
# many RDF clients do not run OWL inference.
###########################################################################

# Scheme scope definitions completed in 0.6.0.
sstim-v:CautionTagScheme skos:definition "Safety, comfort, attention, and context advisories that an implementation can attach to a preset."@en .
sstim-v:ClaimDirectionScheme skos:definition "Categories describing whether a reviewed body of evidence supports, mixes, leaves inconclusive, or refutes an asserted relation."@en .
sstim-v:EffectDirectionScheme skos:definition "Categories describing the observed direction of a measured outcome relative to a comparator."@en .
sstim-v:EvidenceModalityScheme skos:definition "Tags identifying the stimulation modality and evidence-source context in which a result was obtained."@en .
sstim-v:EvidenceTierScheme skos:definition "Ordinal evidence-strength categories used for claim-level assessment rather than technique-wide endorsement."@en .
sstim-v:PermutationFunctionScheme skos:definition "Reordering functions available to cyclic BSC Symmetry note sequences."@en .
sstim-v:PresetGroupScheme skos:definition "BSC implementation categories grouping presets by intended design character and use context."@en .
sstim-v:PublicClaimLevelScheme skos:definition "Ordered ceilings on the kinds of statements allowed in public-facing preset descriptions under SSTIM evidence governance."@en .
sstim-v:ReviewStatusScheme skos:definition "Workflow states describing whether an evidence-tier assignment is provisional, reviewed, or due for reassessment."@en .
sstim-v:SensoryModalityScheme skos:definition "Broad sensory-channel categories used for technique and intervention annotation."@en .
sstim-v:StimulationMechanismScheme skos:definition "Controlled categories for proposed neurobiological and psychophysiological response mechanisms, each requiring separate evidence qualification."@en .
sstim-v:StimulusTemporalStructureScheme skos:definition "Categories describing whether a stimulus is periodic, quasi-periodic, aperiodic, or adaptively controlled."@en .
sstim-v:TechniqueScheme skos:definition "Vendor-neutral catalog of parameterizable auditory, visual, somatosensory, and cross-modal sensory stimulation techniques."@en .
sstim-v:VoiceTypeScheme skos:definition "BSC audio synthesis voice categories used by preset parameter bundles."@en .

